(LAKESHORE STATE UNIVERSITY) Tj T*
(Department of Statistical Science) Tj T*
(STAT 3120: Applied Regression Analysis -- Fall 2026) Tj T*
(Lectures: Tuesday/Thursday 10:10-11:25 am, Halvorsen Hall 140) Tj T*
(Labs: Fridays, sections 201-204 \(see the course site\)) Tj T*
(Course staff: one instructor and three teaching assistants. Office hours are posted on the) Tj T*
(course site.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. COURSE DESCRIPTION) Tj T*
(Linear models for real data: simple and multiple regression, inference for coefficients,) Tj T*
(diagnostics, transformations, model selection, logistic regression and an introduction to) Tj T*
(mixed models. Every topic is taught through a data analysis in R.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prerequisite: STAT 2100 or an equivalent introductory statistics course.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. TEXTS) Tj T*
(- Course notes \(free PDF on the course site\), referred to below as "the Notes".) Tj T*
(- Optional: any recent edition of a standard regression textbook.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. GRADING) Tj T*
(Problem sets \(7, lowest dropped\)    25%) Tj T*
(Midterm 1                           15%) Tj T*
(Midterm 2                           20%) Tj T*
(Final project \(proposal 5%, report 15%\) 20%) Tj T*
(Final exam                          20%) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. PROBLEM SETS) Tj T*
(Problem sets are posted on Monday and are due on Gradebox by 11:59 pm on the Friday listed.) Tj T*
(Late work loses 10% per day, up to three days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Problem Set 1 \(simple regression\) -- due Friday, September 11) Tj T*
(Problem Set 2 \(inference for slopes\) -- due Friday, September 25) Tj T*
(Problem Set 3 \(multiple regression\) -- due Friday, October 9) Tj T*
(Problem Set 4 \(diagnostics and residual plots\) -- due Friday, October 23) Tj T*
(Problem Set 5 \(transformations and interactions\) -- due Friday, October 30) Tj T*
(Problem Set 6 \(model selection\) -- due Friday, November 13) Tj T*
(Problem Set 7 \(logistic regression\) -- due Friday, December 4) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. EXAMS) Tj T*
(Midterm 1 is in class on Thursday, October 1 and covers Notes chapters 1-4.) Tj T*
(Midterm 2 is an evening exam on Thursday, November 5, 7:30-9:00 pm, in Halvorsen Hall 140.) Tj T*
(It covers Notes chapters 5-8. One handwritten formula sheet is allowed.) Tj T*
(The final exam is cumulative: Wednesday, December 16, 2:00-4:30 pm \(room to be announced by the) Tj T*
(registrar\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. FINAL PROJECT) Tj T*
(You will analyze a public data set of your choice in a team of two.) Tj T*
(- Project proposal \(one page: question, data source, planned model\) due Monday, November 2 at) Tj T*
(11:59 pm.) Tj T*
(- Final project report \(8-10 pages with code appendix\) due Friday, December 11 at 11:59 pm.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. READING) Tj T*
(Read Notes chapters 1-2 before the first lab on September 4.) Tj T*
(Before Midterm 2, reread Notes chapter 7 on influence and leverage; it is the most-missed topic) Tj T*
ET
